":"Röst","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Frederick P.","last_name":"Roth","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tian","last_name":"Xia","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Gary D.","last_name":"Bader","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Robbie","last_name":"Loewith","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nicholas G.","last_name":"Davis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Brenda","last_name":"Andrews","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Chad","last_name":"Myers","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jason","last_name":"Moffat","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Charles","last_name":"Boone","orcid":null}],"funders":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01gavpb45","name":"Canadian Institutes of Health Research","grant_id":"MOP_142735"},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","grant_id":"MCB1818293"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01h531d29","name":"Natural Sciences and Engineering Research Council of Canada","grant_id":"RGPIN-2020-04180"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01gavpb45","name":"Canadian Institutes of Health Research","grant_id":"PJT 173542"},{"id":"https://ror.org/000az4664","name":"Canada Foundation for Innovation","grant_id":"39977"},{"id":"https://ror.org/051639p85","name":"Ontario Research Foundation","grant_id":"RE09-011"},{"id":"https://ror.org/051639p85","name":"Ontario Research Foundation","grant_id":"RE011-006"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01gavpb45","name":"Canadian Institutes of Health Research","grant_id":"PJT-180285"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01gavpb45","name":"Canadian Institutes of Health Research","grant_id":"PJT-GMX-463531"},{"id":null,"name":"McLauglin Centre Accelerator","grant_id":"MC-2024-08-02"},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","grant_id":"DFG Bi 2086/1-1"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"R01HG005084"},{"id":null,"name":"McLauglin Centre Accelerator","grant_id":"MC-2022-02"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"R01HG00583"},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","grant_id":"T32GM008347"},{"id":null,"name":"NIH/NCI Ruth L. Kirschstein National Research F30 Award","grant_id":"5F30CA257227"}],"categories":["Genetics","Biological Network"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"835fcfbvhs","title":"Preparation of CRISPR/Cas9 and gRNA plasmids","description":"Human genome engineering has been transformed by the introduction of the CRISPR (clustered regularly interspaced short palindromic repeats)/Cas (CRISPR-associated) system found in most bacteria and archaea. Type II CRISPR/Cas systems have been engineered to induce RNA-guided genome editing in human cells, where small RNAs function together with Cas9 nucleases for sequence-specific cleavage of target sequences. Here we describe the protocol for Cas9-mediated human genome engineering, including construct building and transfection methods necessary for delivering Cas9 and guide RNA (gRNA) into human-induced pluripotent stem cells (hiPSCs) and HEK293 cells. Following genome editing, we also describe methods to assess genome editing effi- ciency using next-generation sequencing and isolate monoclonal hiPSCs with the desired modifications for downstream applications. Keywords: genome engineering • CRISPR • human stem cells","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2016-12-12T12:58:15.307Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/835fcfbvhs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/835fcfbvhs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"George","last_name":"Church","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Experimental Method"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"m8pkzbktbk","title":"Brunello Whole Genome Knock out library in BE(2)-C Neuroblastoma cells - NGS dataset of library population","description":"NGS data to confirm representative and balanced creation of the Brunello whole genome knock out library in BE(2)-C neuroblastoma cells. \nHuman Brunello CRISPR knockout pooled library was a gift from David Root and John Doench (Addgene #73178). \nBE(2)-C cells from ATCC CRL-2268.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-11-01T07:40:29.578Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/m8pkzbktbk","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/m8pkzbktbk"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lisa","last_name":"Francomacaro","orcid":null},{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Neuroblastoma","Genomic Library","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9","Knock Out","CRISPR"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"2v5jg2zksj","title":"TMEM79/MATTRIN defines a pathway for Frizzled regulation and is required for Xenopus embryogenesis","description":"Absctract\nWnt signaling through the Frizzled (FZD) family of serpentine receptors is essential for embryogenesis and homeostasis, and stringent control of the FZD protein level is critical for stem cell regulation. Through CRISPR/Cas9 genome-wide screening in human cells, we identified TMEM79/MATTRIN, an orphan multi-span transmembrane protein, as a specific inhibitor of Wnt/FZD signaling. TMEM79 interacts with FZD during biogenesis and promotes FZD degradation independent of ZNRF3/RNF43 ubiquitin ligases (R-spondin receptors). TMEM79 interacts with ubiquitin-specific protease 8 (USP8), whose activating mutations underlie human tumorigenesis. TMEM79 specifically inhibits USP8 deubiquitination of FZD, thereby governing USP8 substrate specificity and promoting FZD degradation. Tmem79 and Usp8 genes have a pre-bilaterian origin, and Tmem79 inhibition of Usp8 and Wnt signaling is required for anterior neural development and gastrulation in Xenopus embryos. TMEM79 is a predisposition gene for Atopic dermatitis, suggesting deregulation of Wnt/FZD signaling a possible cause for this most common yet enigmatic inflammatory skin disease.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-09-26T05:47:58.606Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/2v5jg2zksj","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/2v5jg2zksj"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Maorong","last_name":"Chen","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Nathalia","last_name":"Amado","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jieqiong","last_name":"Tan","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Alice ","last_name":"Reis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Mengxu","last_name":"Ge","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jose","last_name":"Abreu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Xi","last_name":"He","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Molecular Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"gvygz8cnw9","title":"Calabrese Whole Genome CRISPR Activation library in BE(2)-C Neuroblastoma cells - NGS dataset of library population","description":"NGS data to confirm representative and balanced creation of the Calabrese whole genome activation library sets A and B in BE(2)-C neuroblastoma cells. \nHuman Calabrese CRISPR Activation Pooled Library (Set A and B) was a gift from David Root and John Doench (Addgene #1000000111).\nBE(2)-C cells from ATCC CRL-2268.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-01-06T14:16:14.914Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/gvygz8cnw9","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/gvygz8cnw9"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lisa","last_name":"Francomacaro","orcid":null},{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Neuroblastoma","Genomic Library","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR","CRISPR Activation"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"f7btcr6x6d","title":"A non-canonical function of glutathione to suppress ferroptosis via FSP1","description":"Whole genome-wide CRISPR KO screen","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-10-02T11:41:52.925Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f7btcr6x6d","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f7btcr6x6d"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"BO","last_name":"CHU","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"9x47wzy8x7","title":"A study of \"Genome-wide CRISPR screens reveal host factors critical for SARS-CoV-2 infection\" by Wei et al. Cell 2020","description":"Identification of host genes essential for SARS-CoV-2 infection may reveal novel therapeutic targets and inform our understanding of COVID-19 pathogenesis. Here, we performed genome-wide CRISPR screens in Vero-E6 cells with SARS-CoV-2, MERS-CoV, bat coronavirus HKU5 expressing the SARS-CoV-1 spike, and VSV expressing the SARS-CoV-2 spike. Together this identifies potential therapeutic targets for SARS-CoV-2 and reveals SARS-lineage specific and pan-coronavirus host factors that regulate susceptibility to highly pathogenic coronaviruses.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-10-15T21:29:14.06Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/9x47wzy8x7","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/9x47wzy8x7"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Craig","last_name":"Wilen","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR","Middle East Respiratory Syndrome-Related Coronavirus","Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2","COVID-19"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"wkttx6tp2d","title":"S. aureus transposon sequencing in the murine vaginal tract ","description":"Results from TRANSIT Tn-seq conditional essentiality analysis, associated to the paper \"Genome-wide mutagenesis identifies factors involved in MRSA vaginal colonization \" by Lyon et al. (2025), under review at Cell Reports. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-02-18T22:39:47.454Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/wkttx6tp2d","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/wkttx6tp2d"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Laurie","last_name":"Lyon","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Transposon","Vagina","Mouse Model","Methicillin-Resistant Staphylococcus aureus"],"journal_issn":[]}],"total_records":139827,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":169,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":139827,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":139012,"restricted":71,"embargoed":744},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"National Natural Science Foundation of China","count":2325},{"id":"https://ror.org/01cwqze88","name":"National Institutes of Health","count":706},{"id":"https://ror.org/03ha2q922","name":"National Science Centre","count":478},{"id":"https://ror.org/02ddkpn78","name":"Fundação de Amparo à Pesquisa do Estado de São Paulo","count":432},{"id":"https://ror.org/00x0ma614","name":"Coordenação de Aperfeicoamento de Pessoal de Nível Superior","count":420},{"id":"https://ror.org/03swz6y49","name":"Conselho Nacional de Desenvolvimento Científico e Tecnológico","count":410},{"id":"https://ror.org/021nxhr62","name":"U.S. National Science Foundation","count":404},{"id":"https://ror.org/018mejw64","name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","count":336},{"id":"https://ror.org/00hhkn466","name":"Japan Society for the Promotion of Science","count":280},{"id":"https://ror.org/05r0vyz12","name":"Ministerio de Ciencia, Innovación y Universidades","count":235}],"source_stats":[{"id":"MENDELEY_DATA","name":"Mendeley Data","count":137166},{"id":"f881433a-b1cd-40d2-ab9f-4fd501f2d14b","name":"Elsevier Data Repository","count":1911},{"id":"a191461c-0227-403f-a1e9-621e0e0429cc","name":"San Raffaele Open Research Data Repository","count":187},{"id":"b07018a5-fee6-4df1-9d43-ff0d81ad75ed","name":"Bicocca Open Archive Research Data","count":140},{"id":"df228bbb-ac66-410f-8c66-f61608d63d95","name":"University of South Florida","count":79},{"id":"2a9d1b7d-e447-466f-888f-aa6f